{"name":"Light Detroit","hex":"#cddbdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"detroit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The largest city and former capital of Michigan, United States, a major port on the Detroit River, known as the traditional automotive center of the U.S. It is the county seat of Wayne County.","The United States' automotive industry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detroit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Detroit","blocks":[{"text":"Detroit is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Michigan. It is situated on the bank of the Detroit River across from the Canadian city of Windsor, Ontario. It is the 26th-most populous city in the United States and the largest U.S. city on the Canada–United States border, with a population of 639,111 at the 2020 census, and an estimated 2025 population of 649,095, its first population increase since 1950. The Metro Detroit area, at over 4.4 million people, is the 14th-largest metropolitan area in the nation and second-largest in the Midwest. The county seat of Wayne County, Detroit is a significant cultural center known for its contributions to music, art, architecture, and design, in addition to its historical automotive and industrial background."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Detroit_Skyline_from_Windsor_2025-09-01.jpg/330px-Detroit_Skyline_from_Windsor_2025-09-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detroit","wikidata":"Q12439"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg/500px-Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg/1280px-Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg/500px-Fox_Theater_Restored_to_It%27s_Original_Brilliance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFox_Theater_Restored_to_It's_Original_Brilliance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Ambassador_Bridge_from_the_Detroit_River%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-07-27_01.jpg/500px-Ambassador_Bridge_from_the_Detroit_River%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-07-27_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Amba